<title>UK: Bank Austria sets 3.5 bln Luf zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>Bank Austria sets 3.5 bln Luf zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Credit Europeen and Banque Bruxelles Lambert SA.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK AUSTRIA</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  CITY OF VIENNA</p>
<p> AMT    3.5 BLN LUF   COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    22.DEC.05</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  58.65     PAY DATE 21/22.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    =	   YIELD	 6.05 PCT</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 50-250    SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    1.20	SELL CONC  =	   PRAECIPUUM  0.175</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
